  "common_prompt_original": "Use case: identity-preserve.\nAsset type: production 2D Unity game CHARACTER-ONLY animation sprite sheet.\nInput image: Stand.png is the exact character identity reference. Preserve his exact face, jade-green/gold armor, pale blue-gray skin, red eyes, green horsehair plume, brow gem, gold cloud-scroll patterns, long green tabard, gold-trimmed boots, gigantic jade hammer with gold bands and large inset green face gems and long dark-green handle. Match the reference's strong dark outlines, line weight and detailed cel shading. Maintain three-quarter LEFT-facing orientation and fixed camera. Change poses only, never redesign the character or hammer.\nMANDATORY COMPOSITION: a portrait 1024x1536 RGBA PNG with genuinely transparent alpha background. EXACTLY 16 complete character figures, 4 columns x 4 rows, uniformly spaced at cell origins (0,0),(256,0),(512,0),(768,0), then y=384,768,1152. Each invisible cell is exactly 256x384. Read frames left-to-right, top-to-bottom; time progresses continuously across row breaks.\nEach character AND all equipment must be SMALL inside its own cell: total occupied width at most 178px (70%), total occupied height at most 288px (75%). At least 39px fully transparent horizontal padding at both sides and 40px vertical padding at top and bottom in EVERY cell, including outside canvas edges. Prefer total neutral silhouette height about 190-200px and width about 170px; reserve ample overhead space for raised hammer/leaping actions. Use a single fixed drawing scale across all 16 frames; neutral boot soles are on cell-local ground baseline y=328, body center consistently near local x=140. Grounded hammer rests low at image LEFT. Never enlarge figures to fill the canvas. No sprite or equipment touches a cell boundary, overlaps another sprite, or is cropped. All heads, plumes, armor, boots, hands, handles and complete hammer heads visible every frame.\nNo text, no frame numbers, no labels, no borders, no grid lines, no background, no floor plane, no cast shadows, no separate effects. True transparent empty gutters. Exactly one guard and one hammer per cell.\n",
  "common_prompt_revised": "Create a game animation sprite sheet as a transparent cutout asset. Input Stand.png is a CHARACTER IDENTITY reference only, not a background reference. Use the identical green/gold hammer guard, exact costume, pale blue-gray skin, red eyes, green plume, jade hammer gems and cloud-scroll ornament, detailed cel shading and strong clean dark outlines, three-quarter left-facing.\nCRITICAL CANVAS: 1024 pixels wide by 1536 pixels high. Divide the canvas mentally into FOUR COLUMNS and FOUR ROWS: sixteen invisible 256x384 rectangles. Exactly one full character plus his intact hammer per rectangle, sixteen complete poses total. Pose sequence is row-major left-to-right top-to-bottom.\nCRITICAL SCALE: draw the actual character MUCH SMALLER than normal, like small isolated game icons surrounded by empty air. Neutral full figure including plume and hammer about 164 pixels wide by 190 pixels tall. This leaves a lot of transparent space. Absolute maximum bounding box including equipment per pose is 176 wide and 280 high. Same small drawing scale throughout; do NOT fill cell or sheet. Put each cell-local neutral soles at y=320. Every cell must have AT LEAST 40 pixels EMPTY LEFT AND RIGHT padding and AT LEAST 44 pixels EMPTY TOP AND BOTTOM padding. There must be very wide completely transparent blank vertical AND horizontal gutters between all figures. Everything fits inside its own invisible rectangle. Entire hammer, handle, plume and boots fully visible.\nCRITICAL ALPHA: Actual fully transparent alpha outside sprites, as a transparent PNG asset. Erase ALL background pixels. NO green, brown, gold or black backdrop, NO gradient, NO background color, NO texture, NO checkerboard drawn into the image. NO shadow underneath. Background and gutters are EMPTY transparent pixels, alpha zero. No border, grid, lettering, numbering, FX, trails, dust, ground or floor.\nPreserve body scale across poses even when the hammer raises overhead. Pose only the single character with his hammer.",
